UPDATE bank_soal SET description='Grand Opening of Lorian Public Library

The Lorian Public Library is pleased to announce its grand opening ceremony, which marks the completion of a five-year development project aimed at improving literacy and public education. The new building is located in the heart of the city, making it easily accessible for students, researchers, and community members of all ages. The library is designed to serve as a modern learning hub that combines digital innovation with traditional reading spaces.

The facility features a digital research center equipped with more than seventy computers, interactive boards, and online academic databases. There is also a children’s reading hall with storytelling corners, creative workshops, and weekly literacy programs. For adults, the library offers seminar rooms, language-learning areas, and a silent study zone intended for exam preparation or work-related research.

To celebrate the opening, the library will hold a special ceremony on Saturday, 12 April 2025, starting at 09.00 a.m. The event will include a ribbon-cutting session, a guided tour of the building, and a book donation corner where visitors can contribute books for public use. Several well-known authors from across Indonesia will also attend to give motivational talks and sign copies of their latest works.

Community members are encouraged to join the event and take part in the introductory workshops offered on the same day. Topics include digital literacy, academic writing, and environmental awareness. Registration for these workshops is free but limited to the first one hundred participants. Refreshments will be served throughout the event.

The library management hopes that this new facility will become a center for inclusive learning, creativity, and collaboration. With accessible spaces and diverse programs, the Lorian Public Library aims to inspire people to read more, think critically, and contribute positively to society. Everyone is welcome to participate and experience the new learning environment.

For more information, visitors may contact the library office through the official website or customer hotline available from Monday to Friday, 08.00 a.m. to 04.00 p.m.

